{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Making a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"],"anchor":"Making-a-plan"},{"title":"Writing a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"],"anchor":"Writing-a-plan"},{"title":"Checking a plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"],"anchor":"Checking-a-plan"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplans"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracking-plan.json"},{"type":"text","text":", and for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tools outside the app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand","type":"reference"},{"text":", marked ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@main"},{"text":". It writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"text":". The schemas usually come from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The module is a product of its own that ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"TrackingPlans","role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlans","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlanError":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanError"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackingPlanError"}],"title":"TrackingPlanError","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplanerror","abstract":[{"text":"Why schemas can’t make a tracking plan.","type":"text"}]},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/File":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"File"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"File"}],"title":"TrackingPlan.File","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans\/trackingplan\/file","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One file of a tracking plan: its path within the plan’s directory and its bytes."}]},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/TrackingPlan/check(againstDirectory:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"check(againstDirectory:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"check"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalPa